Not really.  It's still a hack-n-slash adventure based on RPG elements.
There's no support for any of the elaborate "freeform" stuff that an RPG
holds; take #chat for example.  Making #chat do something significant would 
simply be trying to forcibly bolt RPG elements into a game that wasn't designed
to hold them -- it wouldn't change Nethack from a hack-n-slash dungeon
crawl, it would be a hack-n-slash dungeon crawl where you had to push
the button on some monsters to get the benefit.

I believe ADOM spent a great deal of time trying to include RPG-ish
features.  If the OP wants to play a roguelike RPG, ADOM will be far
more suited for him.

